# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the QuantumVerse sanitization pipeline.
#
# Only third-party/system data races that are known teardown/thread-start
# artifacts belong here. Never suppress races originating from src/ - fix those.
#
# Syntax: race:<substring matched against any frame of either race stack>
#
# A suppression fires when ANY frame of EITHER the read or write stack matches
# the pattern, so a pattern here is intentionally library-scoped. Genuine races
# in our own code (physics/math/ml namespaces) never pass through these library
# frames and therefore remain unsuppressed and will still fail the gate.

# Qt races on the global allocator (operator new/delete) inside QThread::start
# when spawning worker threads at startup/teardown. The conflicting access frames
# land in libQt6Core (QThread::start), so this is a Qt-internal teardown race,
# not a QuantumVerse defect.
race:libQt6Core.so.6

# glib (GObject/GLib event loop) reports benign teardown races on its internal
# data structures during Qt/GLib event-loop shutdown (e.g. libglib-2.0.so.0
# offsets). These are library-internal and not QuantumVerse defects.
race:libglib-2.0.so.0
